    "intro_html":  "Beef bourguignon has a reputation for being fussy French cooking, and it is really just a beef stew with bacon, mushrooms, and a mountain of onions cooked down into the gravy. The cut it calls for is chuck, the same cheap roast in every other braise on this site. The name is expensive, the groceries are not. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e47 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and 726 calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e$5.48\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
